      { term: "Executory contract", definition: "A contract under which neither party has performed any of its obligations, or both have partially performed to an equal extent — generally outside IAS 37's scope unless onerous." },
      { term: "Onerous contract", definition: "A contract in which the unavoidable costs of meeting the obligations exceed the economic benefits expected to be received." },
      { term: "Constructive obligation", definition: "An obligation derived from an entity's actions, established pattern of practice, or published policies, creating a valid expectation in others that it will discharge certain responsibilities." }
